# Packages the NixOS package repository holds (hps-starter sync nixos).
# One per line: NAME [OUTPUT], or NAME STORE-PATH. NAME is the nixpkgs package
# name without its version; the release's own store-paths list says which store
# path that is (the one whose closure holds the starter's glibc, that is
# x86_64). With no OUTPUT the default output is meant, else the named one.
# NAME STORE-PATH takes the path as it stands, with no search: for a name the
# release holds in several versions, or a package nixpkgs does not have.
# The repository holds each package's whole closure. ZFS is in the stock
# starter and is not listed. Which node gets which package is
# lib/starter/nixos.roles.
libvirt
qemu-host-cpu-only
open-iscsi
mdadm
targetcli-fb
# The ctrl-exec agent and its executor: a LOCAL package, built by the builder
# (nix/package.nix of ctrl-exec), not in nixpkgs. Its path is put in the local
# area with `hps-starter add-local` (docs/BUNDLE.md "Local packages") and named
# here. A new version is a new line: add-local, change the path, sync, and a node
# takes it at its next bundle-refresh. Its closure holds the Perl modules (JSON is
# the starter's own path) and openssl the agent needs, so none is listed.
ctrl-exec-agent /nix/store/s9s4irf45ylxa3s6cmvl3c6iq9prbq9b-ctrl-exec-agent-0.14.7
# What the storage and compute scripts call and the starter does not have (step 3,
# docs/BUNDLE.md "Storage and compute"). Each is the x86_64 store path the pinned
# images use (upstream, signed by cache.nixos.org), named as it stands so that no
# search is made and the choice among several candidates is not left to a guess.
jq /nix/store/5gzyrb8fdgqcj9qyg0dhz5c20m0k4b78-jq-1.8.2-bin
smartmontools /nix/store/l5ak22wkkiv2mgv3hcp7ihsmhv40mgxk-smartmontools-7.5
tcpdump /nix/store/107bankzjkd6j9s2hnllhl88p5wqcw87-tcpdump-4.99.6
xxd /nix/store/anbhv1x4z9s5xpvpi5v4z2dzq0943ma0-xxd-tinyxxd-1.3.15
# om3 (OpenSVC v3): a LOCAL package, the build the pinned images use (pinned
# v3.0.0-rc62 in flake.nix), from the lab's Nix cache; not in nixpkgs. Put on the
# IPS with `hps-starter add-local nixos --from <cache> <path>` like the agent.
# 3.0.0-rc62 has no upstream signature in the lab cache either, so a node takes it
# unchecked, in its own call.
om3 /nix/store/icpkmfz7s1kdv444l7sfdsvijk7m7qvx-om3-3.0.0-rc62
# AppArmor for the guests (docs/BUNDLE.md "AppArmor"): the parser and the abstractions
# the profiles include, 4.1.7, the store paths of the pinned images (upstream, signed).
apparmor-parser /nix/store/3imv6g6axmczk448vcd0j0jfb6cil7gl-apparmor-parser-4.1.7
apparmor-profiles /nix/store/vi6bapcazps48lkkawiih15f6w660lk4-apparmor-profiles-4.1.7
# The monitoring checks (docs/BUNDLE.md "Monitoring"): two LOCAL packages, the builds
# of the pinned images from the lab's cache, put on the IPS with `hps-starter add-local`.
# nagios-check is the ctrl-exec plugin (one file); hps-nagios-plugins is the directory of
# plugins the pinned node-base image uses (check_disk, check_load, check_procs, check_mem
# are taken from it; the usage checks come from the bundle).
nagios-check /nix/store/ybjld8icqjq1lm0ysscyx0i8xn5dcn0x-nagios-check
hps-nagios-plugins /nix/store/61jhl0q7ydh5mw6cj2xm1j0hyiaqhsds-hps-nagios-plugins
